{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544410-who-is-up-first-character-creation","id":1544410,"title":"Who is up first? [Character Creation]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-21T11:11:10-07:00","id":1544410,"title":"Who is up first? [Character Creation]","content":"Now that the character creation rules have been released, I'm sure a bunch of us are testing systems out by creating characters. Who are you making first? <br /> <br /> (I am waffling a do a couple simultaneous, so I'll share who I actually finish first once I'm done XD)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T12:39:00-07:00","id":1544418,"title":"","content":"I'm working on going through step by step to see how character creation is actually meant to work.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Which I have now done!<br /> <br /> I tried making the &quot;Prom Queen Who Hates Being a Werewolf&quot; character archetype I mentioned on another thread.<br /> <br /> It was an...interesting experience.<br /> <br /> I tried to follow the character creation instructions as they were written, rather than carrying over my assumptions from other games. In particular, this meant picking my Paths (including the Role Path) based on what those Paths represented in-world rather than what stats they gave me. I did this because that honestly seems to be the intent; a lot of what I've been reading as flaws in the system might actually be a consequence of the system genuinely assuming that you don't care about where your dots go very much.<br /> <br /> Taking Primal (Major); Get of Lyka (Minor); Student (Minor) I got the following:<br /> <br /> Artistry 1, Athletics 3, Close Combat 2, Culture 1, Empathy 2, Persuasion 3, Leadership 1, Science 1, Survival 1, Technology 1<br /> <br /> Intellect 2, Cunning 3, Resolve 4; Might 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> <br /> Notably a lot of the character's stats wound up quite similar to Izzy's because obviously most of them come from the Paths and they're all the same.<br /> <br /> I think a particular thing to notice is that I wound up with Resolve 4 not because I particularly imagine this character as being immensely strong-willed but because the system kept giving me points in Mental Attributes and Resolve is the Attribute that feels like it says the least about your character. I didn't particularly want to be extremely intelligent or cunning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":".  A little extra explanation 10-21-2024, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T05:33:58-07:00","id":1544545,"title":"","content":"Absolutely, if you select the same three Paths as one of the pregens you're going to end up with a similar array of Attributes and Skills, but do keep in mind you're free to create your own Role and if you don't feel that's clear, please submit to to the feedback form. Plus, I think there's more variation available than you're making clear.<br /> <br /> Your Attributes<br /> Intellect 2, Cunning 3, Resolve 4; Might 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> <br /> Izzy's Attributes<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Intellect 2, Cunning 4, Resolve 3; Might 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3</span><br /> <br /> Frank's Attributes<br /> Intellect 5, Cunning 2, Resolve 2; Might 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 5; Presence 4, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Alexis's Attributes<br /> Intellect 3, Cunning 2, Resolve 4; Might 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 2; Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> Frank and Alexis are freshly made, but follow the same Attribute breakdowns as your character and Izzy's, yet their splits are different. Your character is built very similarly to Izzy's, but you didn't put 5 dots in anything, or 1 in anything, so naturally that will result in stats averaging out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T07:44:34-07:00","id":1544553,"title":"","content":"Since i got a Chimera on the quizz test a while back i'm thinking about making one, though i'm a bit unsure as to how their true form always bleeding out works, there doesn't seem to be any mechanical effect and the narrative one is a bit vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:56:54-07:00","id":1544575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544410-who-is-up-first-character-creation?p=1544545#post1544545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely, if you select the same three Paths as one of the pregens you're going to end up with a similar array of Attributes and Skills, but do keep in mind you're free to create your own Role and if you don't feel that's clear, please submit to to the feedback form. Plus, I think there's more variation available than you're making clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Variously:<br /> <br /> The fact that selecting the same three Paths gives you a similar array of Attributes and Skills is kind of what I mean by there being customisability issues with the core system because the way the game is set up, two of the three paths are fixed by the <i>kind of supernatural being you want to be</i> and the other one is basically fixed by your character concept. &quot;Werewolf who is in highschool&quot; is, by itself a concept that could cover all kinds of things but &quot;werewolf&quot; defines your Family and Lineage while &quot;who is in highschool&quot; covers the Role so it makes you quite mechanically constrained.<br /> <br /> As for inventing a custom Role, this isn't currently just unclear, there straight-up aren't rules for it. Those rules can be reverse-engineered but, for example, there's no information about what Attribute Arrays are and are not acceptable.<br /> <br /> Finally, yes it's possible to make characters that differ by more than one or two points if you deliberately skew them but that's the kind of white-room exercise that you (quite rightly) suggest we avoid. You still wind up with three characters who are (in old money terms) Physical Primary, Mental Secondary, Social Tertiary which is quite likely to not be what you actually want.<br /> <br /> I'll repeat that <b>none of this is a problem</b> if, as you have suggested elsewhere, the Storyguide chapter provides options for just using free assignment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since i got a Chimera on the quizz test a while back i'm thinking about making one, though i'm a bit unsure as to how their true form always bleeding out works, there doesn't seem to be any mechanical effect and the narrative one is a bit vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly with the current version of the rules &quot;there doesn't seem to be any mechanical effect and the narrative one is a bit vague&quot; is kind of this game's themesong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-23-2024, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T10:22:38-07:00","id":1544891,"title":"","content":"Alright, here are some characters:<br /> <br /> <b>The Runaway</b><br /> <br /> Oksana Rybakova comes from a Russian family of Spawn of Vodnik who settled Alaskan islands in the 1700s. Since that time they have remained relatively isolated, preserving the legacy of Vodnik through incest. Oksana is a 15 year old girl who was to be wed to her much older uncle, a situation not uncommon in the Rybakov family. Not wanting to do this, she fled from her family when she had the chance and traveled to the mainland. She lived on the streets and forests, stealing if she had to, until she runs into the other player characters...<br /> <br /> Lineage: Primal (minor)<br /> Family: Spawn of Vodnik (major)<br /> Role: Criminal<br /> <br /> Intellect 2<br /> Cunning 3<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> Might 2<br /> Dexterity 4<br /> Stamina 4<br /> <br /> Presence 3<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Skills: Athletics 2, Close Combat 2, Empathy 1, Esoterica 2, Larceny 4, Persuasion 1, Pilot 1, Ranged Combat 1, Survival 2<br /> <br /> Spells: Silver Tongue, Precise Transformation, Bestial Voice<br /> <br /> Edges: Nimble Defense 2, Anonymity 1<br /> <br /> Torments: Predator's Colors<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Modern Mendicant</b><br /> <br /> Michael James is a man of deep Christian faith, who felt the calling to give up all of his worldly possessions and to go forth into the world to help others. Since he has sacrificed his old life, he has found that he can work miracles<br /> <br /> Lineage: Sorcerer (minor)<br /> Family: Unburdened (major)<br /> Role: Caregiver<br /> <br /> Intellect 3<br /> Cunning 2<br /> Resolve 4<br /> <br /> Might 2<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 4<br /> <br /> Presence 3<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Composure 4<br /> <br /> Skills: Artistry 1, Athletics 1, Culture 1, Empathy 2, Esoterica 3, Larceny 1, Medicine 2, Persuasion 2, Survival 2, Technology 1<br /> <br /> Spells: Regrowth, Proliferate, Flit<br /> <br /> Edges: Fame 1, Field Medic 2<br /> <br /> Torments: Unchecked Hubris","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T11:26:25-07:00","id":1544897,"title":"","content":"Cool to see some people making characters. Tiny note that I think is worth mentioning because it's easy to miss. It seems like the intent is that Torments have specific triggers, obviously these are sample characters but it *seems* like when you pick a Torment you don't just pick what Torment you have, you also pick what triggers it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T11:55:06-07:00","id":1544898,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I need to go back and reread the Torments section. I\u2019m still a bit hazy on some of these rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:26:45-07:00","id":1544916,"title":"","content":"Here it goes ! Dont have a name for the character or right background/description since i'm not quite sure how the specific damnation of the chimerae works exactly <br /> <br /> <b>The Alchemist</b><br /> <br /> Lineage: Outcast (minor)<br /> Family: Chimera (Major)<br /> Role path : Artificer (Mental 2, Physical 2, Science, Technology, Esoterica)<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> <br /> Intellect 4<br /> Cunning 4<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> Might 2<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 4<br /> <br /> Presence 3<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills: </b><br /> <br /> Artistry 1<br /> Athletics 1<br /> Close combat 2<br /> Culture 1<br /> Enigmas 2<br /> Esoterica 2<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Medicine 3<br /> Science 2<br /> Technology 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edges:</b><br /> Unusually secured quarter 1<br /> Empty bowl 3<br /> Resources 1<br /> <br /> <b>Spells:<br /> <br /> Motif : </b>When casting spells from the Summoning Manifestation, bleed one less curse die to a minimum of zero.<br /> <br /> - Assistive construct<br /> - Burning Halo<br /> - Weaponmaster's skills<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Torments :</b><br /> <br /> Lineage<br /> Show of Force <br /> (having my skills doubted)<br /> <br /> Personal <br /> Gain someone's affection (Witnessing a religious ceremony)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T11:02:23-08:00","id":1545747,"title":"","content":"Finally finished mine!<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Max Walker</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b>: An airline steward who got Final Destination-ed - but being persued by Death (an Outsider? An Archon?) infused them with the energies of Death.<br /> <br /> <b>Lineage: </b>Dead (Empathy, Esoterica, Survival; Mental 1, Physical 1, Social 2)<br /> <b>Family (Major):</b> Poltergeist (Larceny, Pilot, Technology; Mental 5, Physical 2, Social 3)<br /> <b>Role:</b> Airline Steward (Culture, Leadership, Persuasion; Physical 2, Social 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Close Combat 1, Culture 1 (Role), Empathy 2 (Lineage), Escoterica 1 (Lineage), Larceny 1 (Family), Leadership 1 (Role), Medicine 1, Persuasion 2 (Role), Pilot 3 (Family), Survival 1 (Lineage), Technology 2 (Family)<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intellect \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Cunning \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022; Might \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022, Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022; Presence \u2022\u2022\u2022, Manipulation \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Inheritance:</b> Incorporeal Dread<br /> <b>Torments:</b> Corporial Longing ; Provoke fear of death and the future<br /> <b>Lineage Damnation:</b> Dead Urges<br /> <b>Contacts:</b> Steven Hopper, paranormal videographer (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Informant, Investigator, Sneaky); Jennifer Magnus, Dead Countess (\u2022 , Mentor); Captain Kelly, pilot who pretends he doesn't see weird things at 30000 feet (\u2022, Security Clearence)<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Determined Silence, Heirloom (Mutable ID), Quick Read, Resources 2<br /> <b>Practices:</b> Emotional Manipulation, Incorporiality, Metaphysics<br /> <b>Spells:</b> Dissonance, Memoryscape, Nightmares<br /> <b>Motifs:</b> Liminal Power<br /> <b>Defence:</b> 1<br /> <b>Entanglement:</b> 1<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 1<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}